-- the first verdict: exchanging the two hydrogens is not a rotation of the arrangement, so it is not an
-- automorphism of the molecule with its configuration. The two hydrogens of a methylene group next to a
-- stereocentre are therefore distinct positions — diastereotopic — and this is derived from the
-- configuration rather than assigned to the atoms.
cyc-swap-differs : cyc nb-h1 nb-h2 nb-cs ≡ cyc nb-h2 nb-h1 nb-cs → Empty
cyc-swap-differs q = transport (λ i → isTrue (cyc-sign (q i))) unit
